---
title: Din Tai Fung Cucumber Salad
source: https://platingsandpairings.com/din-tai-fung-cucumber-salad-recipe
prep time: 4 hours
servings: 3
tags: asian cucumber salad, cucumber salad, din tai fung, side dishes
course: Salad
cuisine: Taiwanese
image: https://www.platingsandpairings.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/08/din-tai-fung-cucumber-salad-recipe-7-scaled.jpg
---

Add @English cucumbers{2}(sliced into 1/2-inch thick pieces) to a #small bowl{}.

Sprinkle with @kosher salt{1.5%tbsp} and toss to combine. Let sit for ~{30%minutes} in the refrigerator.

Rinse off the salt mixture and pat the cucumbers dry.

Meanwhile, make the dressing. In a #small bowl{}, whisk together @rice vinegar{3%tbsp}, @mirin{1.5%tbsp}, @sugar{2%tbsp}, @sesame oil{1.5%tbsp}, @garlic{3%cloves}(grated or minced, about 1tbsp for 3 cloves), and @kosher salt{1/2%teaspoon}. Mix well and set aside.

Toss the rinsed and dried cucumbers with the dressing and let marinate for a minimum of ~{4%hours}, up to ~{2%days}.

To serve: Taste for seasoning, and add additional @kosher salt{} if needed. Drizzle with @chili oil{1/2%tbsp}(or more, to taste) and sprinkle with @?fresno chile pepper{1}(minced) and serve chilled.

> The originally recipe called for 8 persian cucumbers at base, but these weren't easily found, so we swapped to English cucumbers.